# Wave 46 §B — a corrected copy of `w41-planeswalker.state` (never edited: the
# brief says reuse it read-only, and it is reused elsewhere). That file's
# `aibattlefield=Jace Beleren` carries no `|Counters:LOYALTY=N`, and
# `GameState.applyToGame`'s own puzzle-file placement
# (`GameState.java`'s `processCardsForZone`) does not special-case a
# planeswalker's starting loyalty — it ONLY sets counters from an explicit
# `|Counters:...` suffix (`applyCountersToGameEntity`). Left at the default
# (zero), Forge's own state-based action (`GameAction.java`, "a planeswalker
# with loyalty 0 or less goes to its owner's graveyard") removes Jace almost
# immediately, before this e2e spec ever gets a chance to drag an attacker
# onto it — confirmed empirically (this fixture's Jace never appears on bob's
# battlefield at all; `w43-planeswalker.state` already carries the same
# `|Counters:LOYALTY=N` fix for the identical reason, and says so in its own
# header). `e2e/w46-attack.spec.ts` uses this file, not `w41-planeswalker.state`.
turn=1
activeplayer=human
activephase=MAIN1
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=
humanbattlefield=Memnite
humanlibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humangraveyard=
aihand=
aibattlefield=Jace Beleren|Counters:LOYALTY=3
ailibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
aigraveyard=
